      },
      "payload": {
        "finding_id": "F-001",
        "reason": "Refuted empirically. WorkflowEvent.from_mapping (events.py:145) calls _validate_event_mapping(value) at line 148 BEFORE indexing any key; that helper raises EventPersistenceError for missing/invalid fields, which collect_waivers already catches. Probed all four corruption shapes against the real store - '{}', '[1, 2, 3]', an object with wrong-typed fields, and malformed JSON - and collect_waivers returned {} for every one, raising nothing. The finding's premise that from_mapping reaches value['event_id'] and raises KeyError/TypeError is incorrect. Additionally '[1, 2, 3]' never reaches from_mapping at all: _decode_events rejects a non-Mapping with EventPersistenceError at events.py:192."
      },
      "previous_event_hash": "5f3030e4232e5f6f45955c602d3836b2f1a20b38fe183d53ca4da4cfc0690592",
